      body with same-length spaces before scanning, so the scanner sees no
      command positions there while every computed offset still indexes into
      the original string that gets spliced back. Handles quoted and unquoted
      delimiters, `<<-` tab-stripped terminators, and leaves `<<<` here-strings
      alone. Reproduced the bug with the fix reverted, then confirmed it gone:
      5 new regression assertions, `prefer-rtk-shape: 42 passed, 0 failed`.

### README orientation + animated Graphify visual (2026-07-31, 20:00 PST)

- [x] **[P3]** **Decide whether the graph visual needs a CI gate.** Decided
      yes, and shipped 2026-07-31 (21:00 PST). The original reasoning below
      still holds for the part that was rejected — no Puppeteer job, because
      headless-Chrome checks prove *platform* behaviour rather than repo logic.
      What shipped instead is a cheap artifact lint: `tools/graph-visual.mjs
      --verify` (`npm run check:graph`) re-checks the **committed bytes** of
      both SVGs, wired as a **blocking** step in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`'s
      `docs-links` job. It lints rather than rebuild-and-diffs because
      `renderSvg` bakes the source commit into `<desc>`, so a fresh build at
      CI's `HEAD` is legitimately different bytes and byte-equality would fail
      every PR. `graphify.yml` stays advisory (`continue-on-error: true`) and is
      deliberately not the gate. Original rationale: the invariants that can
      regress (title/desc/`role="img"` present, reduced-motion fallback on the
      animated variant, no keyframes or SMIL in the static twin, 220 kB ceiling)
      were already self-asserted at write time — the gap was that nothing
      re-checked bytes already committed (hand edit, bad merge, truncation).

- [x] **[P3]** **Refresh the visual when the graph moves meaningfully.**
      Automated 2026-07-31 (21:00 PST). `.githooks/pre-commit` now re-renders
      both SVGs from the existing `graphify-out/graph.json` and stages them
      whenever a commit touches `docs/`, `app/`, `website/src/`, `tools/`, or
      `scripts/`, so the committed picture can no longer go stale. The note
      below about `.githooks/post-commit` still stands and is why the render
      lives in **pre**-commit: only the ~1s SVG render runs there, while the
      graph rebuild stays in `post-commit`. The picture is therefore captioned
      "at commit &lt;sha&gt;" of the previous commit, by design.

